<title>USA: Ginnie Mae increases REMIC 1996-24 to $400 mln.</title>
<headline>Ginnie Mae increases REMIC 1996-24 to $400 mln.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Government National Mortgage Association (GNMA) (Ginnie Mae) said it increased to $400 million its Real Estate Mortgage Investment Conduit (REMIC) 1996-24.</p>
<p>The 7.5-percent REMIC priced Oct 29 was increased Nov 13 and has a settlement date of Nov 29, Ginnie Mae said.</p>
<p>The issue is sponsored by PaineWebber Group Inc and Blaylock &amp; Partners L.P., the agency said.</p>
<p>--N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
